module

public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Blowup.Defs

/-!
# Ideals of `R` on an affine chart of a blowup

Let `R` be a ring, let `I ⊆ R` be an ideal, let `a ∈ I` and let `S` be a localization of `R`
away from `a`, so that `R' = R[I/a] = affineBlowupAlgebra I a S` is one of the standard affine
charts of the blowup of `R` in `I`. On that chart the ideal `I` becomes principal, generated by
the image of `a`, and consequently every ideal `J` of `R` contained in a power `I ^ d`
*factors* on the chart: its extension to `R'` is the `d`-th power of the extension of `I`
times the ideal generated by the fractions `x / aᵈ`, `x ∈ J`.

That factorization is the local form of the global statement that the inverse image of such a
`J` under a blowup `b : X' → X` is the `d`-th power of the exceptional ideal times a second
ideal on `X'`: the first factor is `(I · 𝒪_{X'})ᵈ`, read on the chart as `(a)ᵈ`, and the second
factor is the *normalization* `J / aᵈ` of `J`, which is exactly the ideal generated by the
fractions `x / aᵈ`.

## Main definitions

* `affineBlowupAlgebra.fraction I a d` sends `x ∈ Iᵈ` to the fraction `x / aᵈ` of `R[I/a]`.
* `affineBlowupAlgebra.normalize I a d J hJ` is the ideal of `R[I/a]` generated by the
  fractions `x / aᵈ` for `x ∈ J`, for an ideal `J ⊆ Iᵈ`.

## Main results

* `affineBlowupAlgebra.invSelf_pow_mul_algebraMap_mem`: the fraction `x / aⁿ` lies in `R[I/a]`
  for every `x ∈ Iⁿ`, which is what makes `fraction` well defined.
* `affineBlowupAlgebra.algebraMap_pow_mul_fraction`: multiplying `x / aᵈ` by `aᵈ` returns `x`.
  This single identity is what makes the two spans in the factorization match generator by
  generator.
* `affineBlowupAlgebra.map_ideal_eq_span_singleton`: `I · R[I/a] = a · R[I/a]`.
* `affineBlowupAlgebra.map_ideal_pow_eq_span_singleton`: `Iᵈ · R[I/a] = aᵈ · R[I/a]`.
* `affineBlowupAlgebra.map_ideal_eq_span_singleton_mul_normalize`: for `J ⊆ Iᵈ` the extension
  of `J` is `aᵈ` times the normalization of `J`.
* `affineBlowupAlgebra.map_ideal_eq_map_pow_mul_normalize`: the same factorization with the
  first factor written as the `d`-th power of the extension of `I`, which is the shape the
  inverse-image formula for a blowup is stated in.

## Implementation notes

The fractions are written multiplicatively as `invSelf a ^ n * algebraMap R S x` rather than as
`IsLocalization.mk' S x ⟨aⁿ, _⟩`, because the two facts the factorization needs — that the
fraction lies in the subalgebra, and that `aᵈ` times it is `x` — are both multiplicative
identities in `S` and need no manipulation of denominators.

Membership of `x / aⁿ` in `R[I/a]` is proved by induction on `n` from the generators: `R[I/a]`
is `Algebra.adjoin R` of the fractions `y / a` with `y ∈ I`, and an element of `I ^ (n + 1)` is
a sum of products `y · z` with `y ∈ I` and `z ∈ Iⁿ`, whose fraction factors as
`(y / a) · (z / aⁿ)`. The same statement for the model of `R[I/a]` built in
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Blowup/Basic.lean` is `invSelf_pow_mul_mem_affineBlowup`; it is reproved
here for `affineBlowupAlgebra`, which takes the localization `S` abstractly instead of fixing it
to `Localization.Away a`, since no comparison of the two models is available.

`affineBlowupAlgebra.fraction` takes an element of the submodule `↥(I ^ d)` rather than an
element of `R` together with a membership proof, so that the generating set of the
normalization is the range of a function and `Ideal.span_mul_span` applies to it directly. It
is not packaged as an `R`-linear map: the factorization needs only the multiplicative identity
`aᵈ · (x / aᵈ) = x`, and additivity of `x ↦ x / aᵈ` is never used.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached to `map_ideal_eq_span_singleton`. It is part (2) of
Tag 07Z3, which is already formalized, for the quotient-of-representatives model of `R[I/a]`,
as `blowup_idealMap_eq_span` in `StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Blowup/Basic.lean`; this is the same
assertion for the subalgebra model, and attaching the tag again would put two declarations in
the covering set of one clause. The factorization results carry no tag either: in the Stacks
Project they occur inside the proof of Tag 080B (composition of blowups is a blowup) rather than
as statements of their own.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 052Q](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/052Q), the affine blowup
  algebra.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07Z3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07Z3), part (2) of which is
  `affineBlowupAlgebra.map_ideal_eq_span_singleton`.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 080B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/080B), in whose proof the
  factorization of an ideal `J ⊆ Iᵈ` on the charts of the blowup is used.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace affineBlowupAlgebra

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {S : Type*} [CommRing S] [Algebra R S]

section Fraction

variable (I : Ideal R) (a : R) [IsLocalization.Away a S]

/-- The fraction `y / a` lies in `R[I/a]` for every `y ∈ I`: these are its generators. -/
theorem invSelf_mul_algebraMap_mem {y : R} (hy : y ∈ I) :
    IsLocalization.Away.invSelf (S := S) a * algebraMap R S y ∈ affineBlowupAlgebra I a S := by
  refine Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨y, hy, ?_⟩
  refine (IsLocalization.Away.algebraMap_isUnit (S := S) a).mul_left_cancel ?_
  rw [← mul_assoc, IsLocalization.Away.mul_invSelf, one_mul]
  exact (IsLocalization.mk'_spec' S y ⟨a, Submonoid.mem_powers a⟩).symm

/-- The fraction `x / aⁿ` lies in `R[I/a]` for every `x ∈ Iⁿ`. -/
theorem invSelf_pow_mul_algebraMap_mem {n : ℕ} {x : R} (hx : x ∈ I ^ n) :
    IsLocalization.Away.invSelf (S := S) a ^ n * algebraMap R S x ∈
      affineBlowupAlgebra I a S := by
  induction n generalizing x with
  | zero => simp
  | succ n ih =>
    rw [pow_succ'] at hx
    refine Submodule.mul_induction_on hx (fun y hy z hz => ?_) fun u v hu hv => ?_
    · have hfac : IsLocalization.Away.invSelf (S := S) a ^ (n + 1) * algebraMap R S (y * z) =
          (IsLocalization.Away.invSelf (S := S) a * algebraMap R S y) *
            (IsLocalization.Away.invSelf (S := S) a ^ n * algebraMap R S z) := by
        rw [map_mul]; ring
      exact hfac ▸ mul_mem (invSelf_mul_algebraMap_mem I a hy) (ih hz)
    · rw [map_add, mul_add]
      exact add_mem hu hv

/-- The fraction `x / aᵈ` of an element `x ∈ Iᵈ`, as an element of `R[I/a]`. -/
noncomputable def fraction (d : ℕ) (x : ↥(I ^ d)) : affineBlowupAlgebra I a S :=
  ⟨IsLocalization.Away.invSelf a ^ d * algebraMap R S x,
    invSelf_pow_mul_algebraMap_mem I a x.2⟩

/-- The fraction `x / aᵈ`, viewed in `S`, is `a⁻ᵈ · x`. -/
@[simp]
theorem fraction_coe (d : ℕ) (x : ↥(I ^ d)) :
    (fraction (S := S) I a d x : S) =
      IsLocalization.Away.invSelf a ^ d * algebraMap R S x :=
  rfl

/-- In `S`, `aᵈ · (1 / aᵈ) = 1`. -/
private theorem algebraMap_pow_mul_invSelf_pow (d : ℕ) :
    algebraMap R S a ^ d * IsLocalization.Away.invSelf a ^ d = 1 := by
  simp [← mul_pow]

/-- Multiplying the fraction `x / aᵈ` by `aᵈ` returns `x`. -/
theorem algebraMap_pow_mul_fraction (d : ℕ) (x : ↥(I ^ d)) :
    algebraMap R (affineBlowupAlgebra I a S) a ^ d * fraction I a d x =
      algebraMap R (affineBlowupAlgebra I a S) x := by
  refine Subtype.ext ?_
  show algebraMap R S a ^ d * (IsLocalization.Away.invSelf a ^ d * algebraMap R S x) = _
  rw [← mul_assoc, algebraMap_pow_mul_invSelf_pow, one_mul]
  rfl

/-- The fraction `aᵈ / aᵈ` is `1`. -/
theorem fraction_pow_self (ha : a ∈ I) (d : ℕ) :
    fraction (S := S) I a d ⟨a ^ d, Ideal.pow_mem_pow ha d⟩ = 1 := by
  refine Subtype.ext ?_
  simpa [mul_comm] using algebraMap_pow_mul_invSelf_pow (S := S) a d

end Fraction

section Factorization

variable (I J : Ideal R) (a : R) [IsLocalization.Away a S]

/-- **The center becomes principal on an affine chart of the blowup:** for `a ∈ I` the extension
of `I` to `R[I/a]` is generated by the image of `a`. This is part (2) of Stacks Tag 07Z3, for the
subalgebra model of `R[I/a]`. -/
theorem map_ideal_eq_span_singleton (ha : a ∈ I) :
    I.map (algebraMap R (affineBlowupAlgebra I a S)) =
      Ideal.span {algebraMap R (affineBlowupAlgebra I a S) a} := by
  refine le_antisymm (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun x hx => ?_) (Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_)
  · rw [Ideal.mem_comap, Ideal.mem_span_singleton]
    refine ⟨fraction I a 1 ⟨x, by simpa using hx⟩, ?_⟩
    simpa using (algebraMap_pow_mul_fraction I a 1 ⟨x, by simpa using hx⟩).symm
  · rintro _ rfl
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha

/-- For `a ∈ I` the extension of `Iᵈ` to `R[I/a]` is generated by the image of `aᵈ`. -/
theorem map_ideal_pow_eq_span_singleton (ha : a ∈ I) (d : ℕ) :
    (I ^ d).map (algebraMap R (affineBlowupAlgebra I a S)) =
      Ideal.span {algebraMap R (affineBlowupAlgebra I a S) a ^ d} := by
  rw [Ideal.map_pow, map_ideal_eq_span_singleton I a ha, Ideal.span_singleton_pow]

/-- The normalization `J / aᵈ` of an ideal `J ⊆ Iᵈ`: the ideal of `R[I/a]` generated by the
fractions `x / aᵈ` for `x ∈ J`. -/
noncomputable def normalize (d : ℕ) (hJ : J ≤ I ^ d) :
    Ideal (affineBlowupAlgebra I a S) :=
  Ideal.span (Set.range fun x : J => fraction I a d ⟨x, hJ x.2⟩)

/-- **The factorization of an ideal `J ⊆ Iᵈ` on an affine chart of the blowup**, with the first
factor written as the principal ideal `(aᵈ)`: the extension of `J` to `R[I/a]` is `aᵈ` times the
normalization `J / aᵈ`. No relation between `a` and `I` is needed. -/
theorem map_ideal_eq_span_singleton_mul_normalize (d : ℕ) (hJ : J ≤ I ^ d) :
    J.map (algebraMap R (affineBlowupAlgebra I a S)) =
      Ideal.span {algebraMap R (affineBlowupAlgebra I a S) a ^ d} *
        normalize I J a d hJ := by
  rw [normalize, Ideal.span_mul_span, Ideal.map]
  congr 1
  ext z
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨_, Set.mem_singleton _, _, ⟨⟨x, hx⟩, rfl⟩,
      algebraMap_pow_mul_fraction I a d ⟨x, hJ hx⟩⟩
  · rintro ⟨_, rfl, _, ⟨x, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨x, x.2, (algebraMap_pow_mul_fraction I a d ⟨x, hJ x.2⟩).symm⟩

/-- **The factorization of an ideal `J ⊆ Iᵈ` on an affine chart of the blowup.** For `a ∈ I` the
extension of `J` to `R[I/a]` is the `d`-th power of the extension of `I` times the normalization
`J / aᵈ`. This is the chart-local form of the formula `b⁻¹J = (I · 𝒪_{X'})ᵈ · (J / Iᵈ)` for the
inverse image of `J` under the blowup of `I`. -/
theorem map_ideal_eq_map_pow_mul_normalize (ha : a ∈ I) (d : ℕ) (hJ : J ≤ I ^ d) :
    J.map (algebraMap R (affineBlowupAlgebra I a S)) =
      I.map (algebraMap R (affineBlowupAlgebra I a S)) ^ d * normalize I J a d hJ := by
  rw [map_ideal_eq_span_singleton I a ha, Ideal.span_singleton_pow]
  exact map_ideal_eq_span_singleton_mul_normalize I J a d hJ

/-- The normalization of `Iᵈ` itself is the unit ideal, so the factorization is not degenerate:
its second factor is `⊤` exactly in the case `J = Iᵈ`, where the first factor already accounts
for the whole extension. -/
theorem normalize_self (ha : a ∈ I) (d : ℕ) :
    normalize I (I ^ d) a d le_rfl = (⊤ : Ideal (affineBlowupAlgebra I a S)) := by
  refine Ideal.eq_top_of_isUnit_mem _
    (Ideal.subset_span ⟨⟨a ^ d, Ideal.pow_mem_pow ha d⟩, rfl⟩) ?_
  show IsUnit (fraction (S := S) I a d ⟨a ^ d, Ideal.pow_mem_pow ha d⟩)
  rw [fraction_pow_self I a ha d]
  exact isUnit_one

end Factorization

end affineBlowupAlgebra
